# 5. Real-Time Synchronization

The QKMS pages must remain synchronized in real time.

Use the existing SSE/realtime infrastructure where available.

When a key-related event occurs, the appropriate pages must update automatically.

Examples:

### New Key Discovered

Inventory updates
→ Overview updates
→ Risk Analysis recalculates
→ Lifecycle records the key
→ Readiness evaluates PQC posture

### Key Rotated

Rotation Center updates
→ Lifecycle updates
→ Inventory updates key version
→ Risk Analysis updates
→ Governance audit evidence updates

### Key Expires

Lifecycle updates
→ Rotation Center marks key as due/overdue
→ Risk Analysis increases risk if appropriate
→ Overview updates metrics

### Key Migrated to PQC

Readiness updates
→ Inventory updates algorithm
→ Risk Analysis recalculates
→ Overview updates PQC posture
→ Migration status updates

### Policy Changed

Governance updates
→ affected keys are re-evaluated
→ risk posture updates
→ readiness gates update where applicable

